  "method": "One warmed resident checkpoint. Each sample uses a fresh required in-memory cache. Order rotates across modes; CPU thread count is four. Every code sample creates a fresh sandbox process, so timing includes its startup, JSON IPC, validation and host work. Classic samples call the same validated functions directly. JSON response bytes exclude MCP envelopes and are not token counts. No LLM or remote-network round trips are simulated. Two-stage uses dependent awaiting and returns a compact result; classic batching already needs only two calls. Nearest-rank latency percentiles; at three samples p95/p99 are maxima. Input throughput counts initial records, not follow-up questions. Peak memory is not measured. Small sample, uncontrolled workstation load; no general speed claim."
